The conversation focused on a case study detailing fiscal benefits of Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) in Nigeria, highlighting extensive flood-related economic losses, which caused damages of around US$6.68 billion in 2022. Key details included the rising flood risk due to urbanization and climate change, the effectiveness of IWRM in reducing costs through strategic governance and infrastructure investments, and examples of successful IWRM applications in Nigeria. The discussion culminated in synthesizing a message about IWRM's value in mitigating financial risks and attracting investment, tailored for Ministries of Finance to emphasize the financial rationale for sustainable flood risk management strategies.
